# Architecture Rules

## Directory Layout

```
lib/
  core/                         # Shared infrastructure — importable anywhere
    constants/                  # Compile-time constants (AppConstants)
    di/                         # App-wide Riverpod providers (providers.dart)
    errors/                     # Shared exception types (ApiException)
    logging/                    # Talker singleton
    network/                    # DioClient + interceptors
    router/                     # GoRouter definition (appRouterProvider)
    storage/                    # SecureStorageService
  features/<name>/              # Vertical slice — one folder per feature
    data/
      datasources/              # Remote & local data sources (Dio calls, cache)
      models/                   # JSON-serializable DTOs (fromJson / toJson)
      repositories/             # Repository implementations
    domain/
      entities/                 # Plain Dart classes — no framework dependencies
      repositories/             # Abstract repository interfaces
      usecases/                 # Single-responsibility use cases (one `call` method)
    presentation/
      screens/                  # Full screens (Scaffold + AppBar)
      widgets/                  # Feature-scoped widgets
      providers/                # Feature-scoped @riverpod providers
  shared/
    widgets/                    # Reusable widgets — no feature coupling
```

## Hard Rules

1. **Riverpod 3 only** for state — no Bloc, no get_it, no Provider, no ChangeNotifier.
2. **Dio only** for networking — no `http` package.
3. **go_router only** for navigation — no Navigator.push calls in business logic.
4. **No design tokens** — use `ThemeData(useMaterial3: true)` defaults; no custom token files.
5. **Dependency flow**: `presentation → domain ← data`. Data and presentation never import each other.
6. `core/` may be imported by anyone. Features must **not** import each other directly.
7. App-wide singletons live in `core/di/providers.dart`. Feature-scoped providers live in `features/<name>/presentation/providers/`.
8. Use `@Riverpod(keepAlive: true)` only for true singletons (DioClient, SecureStorage, GoRouter). Feature providers are auto-disposed by default.

